From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:48:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Compute sqrt with frsqrte on PowerPC

Without fsqrt the generic sqrt computes one bit at a time. Refine the
frsqrte estimate with Newton steps and round it correctly with
Tuckerman's test using fmsub, sqrtf rounds the double result. Use fsqrt
when the CPU has it.
---
 libm/machine/powerpc/CMakeLists.txt |  2 +
 libm/machine/powerpc/meson.build    |  2 +
 libm/machine/powerpc/s_sqrt.c       | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libm/machine/powerpc/sf_sqrt.c      | 21 +++++++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libm/machine/powerpc/s_sqrt.c
 create mode 100644 libm/machine/powerpc/sf_sqrt.c

diff --git a/libm/machine/powerpc/CMakeLists.txt b/libm/machine/powerpc/CMakeLists.txt
index 1ddda27..b38d3fe 100644
--- a/libm/machine/powerpc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libm/machine/powerpc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -35,4 +35,6 @@
 
 picolibc_sources(
   complex128.c
+  s_sqrt.c
+  sf_sqrt.c
   )
diff --git a/libm/machine/powerpc/meson.build b/libm/machine/powerpc/meson.build
index c2fac2d..22ef6bd 100644
--- a/libm/machine/powerpc/meson.build
+++ b/libm/machine/powerpc/meson.build
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@
 #
 
 srcs_libm_machine = [
